micro-ecc, vendored unchanged for libu2f's P-256 (issue #420).

Source:  https://github.com/kmackay/micro-ecc
Commit:  76fda53af41aed0a5b372227be65f69fcb502400
Licence: BSD 2-clause (LICENSE.txt), compatible with the GPLv3 project.
Files:   uECC.c uECC.h uECC_vli.h curve-specific.inc platform-specific.inc
         types.h asm_arm*.inc LICENSE.txt (examples, tests, build scripts
         and the AVR code left out).

Built only through ../p256.c, which sets the options (secp256r1 only, no
assembler: uECC_arch_other, so r9, the PIC base of MINIX user programs,
is never touched) and the random source.  Older stock firmware used this
library for U2F (lib/micro-ecc); Unleashed uses mbedtls, which is far
larger.
